.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 26, 2026
.Dt PWD_MKDB 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm pwd_mkdb
.Nd install the account database
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl Cp
.Op Fl d Ar directory
.Op Fl u Ar user
.Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility checks
.Ar file ,
a new account database in the
.Pa master.passwd
format described in
.Xr passwd 5 ,
and installs it as
.Pa /etc/master.passwd
with mode 0600.
With
.Fl p ,
it also generates the public
.Pa /etc/passwd ,
in which every password is replaced by
.Ql *
and the class, change and expire fields are left out.
.Pp
Unlike the other BSDs'
.Nm ,
it writes no hashed database files: the C library reads the text files
directly.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl C
Only check
.Ar file ;
install nothing.
.It Fl d Ar directory
Install into
.Ar directory
instead of
.Pa /etc .
.It Fl p
Generate
.Pa passwd
as well.
.It Fl u Ar user
Accepted for compatibility; the whole database is rebuilt.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/master.passwd -compact
.It Pa /etc/master.passwd
the account database
.It Pa /etc/passwd
its public form
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr passwd 1 ,
.Xr passwd 5
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
utility appeared in
.Bx 4.3 Reno .
This implementation was written for OxideBSD.
